This repository and every build distributed through it are PROPRIETARY and are not
open source. They are published for one purpose only: letting approved testers run and
evaluate S4Studio and report problems to support the original project.

1. Grant of use
   You may download and run a sealed build only if you hold a team-signed tester key,
   and only for the validity of that key (one week from the signed expiry date). The key
   is personal, single-use, and non-transferable.

2. No reuse, no derivative works
   You may not copy, modify, adapt, translate, decompile, disassemble, reverse engineer,
   or create derivative works from the builds, the installer, the sealed payload, the
   documentation or any asset of this repository, except where such restriction is
   prohibited by applicable law.

3. No redistribution
   You may not host, mirror, fork, re-upload, resell, sublicense or otherwise
   redistribute this repository, its assets or the builds, in whole or in part, nor use
   them to build or run another product or service. Forks and copies are not licensed
   for any use and must not be used to distribute builds.

4. No circumvention
   You may not bypass, disable or alter the license gate, the signature checks, the
   integrity seal or the self-removal (purge) behavior of the tester builds.

5. Termination
   The license ends automatically at the signed expiry of the key, or immediately on
   revocation. On expiry or revocation the build removes itself: the installation, the
   application data and every artifact derived from the project are deleted and are not
   recoverable. Original game client files and user sources are never touched.

6. No warranty
   The builds are alpha software provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, to the
   maximum extent permitted by law. Test only on servers and databases you own or are
   authorized to use.

7. Reporting
   Security issues, leaked keys and unauthorized copies: open a private report through
   the repository's security contact, or email the maintainer listed in the profile.
   Leaked keys are revoked.

Technical honesty: a public Git repository can always be cloned, and no license can
technically prevent that. What is enforceable is this license, the absence of source
code in this repository, and the fact that a build without a valid team-signed key does
not run. If you find a copy that claims otherwise, it is unauthorized: report it.
